+# CHHHS research intelligence demonstration pilot
+
+## Purpose
+
+This Track 36 vertical slice tests whether Searchright can support a bounded,
+self-hosted institutional publication-monitoring use case. It searches four free
+metadata APIs, deduplicates candidate records, applies conservative institution
+attribution and explainable thematic classification, and produces a monthly
+report bundle.
+
+## Staging
+
+1. **Fixture-only local demonstration.** Run the rights-clear synthetic corpus,
+   inspect every attribution class and confirm that Cairns-only geographic
+   references are excluded.
+2. **Retrospective calibration.** Compare candidate discovery with an
+   adjudicated internal CHHHS publication list. Freeze the institution profile,
+   labelling protocol and thresholds before measuring results.
+3. **Institution self-hosting.** Execute opt-in live searches in a controlled
+   CHHHS environment, retain receipts and state, and require human release of
+   reports.
+4. **Operational decision.** Continue, revise or stop only after data,
+   methodological, security, usability and workload exit criteria are reviewed.
+
+Remote multi-tenant deployment and autonomous publication are outside this
+pilot.
+
+## Attribution policy
+
+Structured metadata containing the governed canonical HHS name, a current
+alias or a verified durable identifier may support confirmed attribution.
+Facility and historical names support probable attribution and remain
+reviewable. Organisation names found only in titles, abstracts or subjects enter
+review rather than the attributed portfolio. “Cairns” by itself is never
+institutional evidence.
+
+The outcome describes metadata attribution only. It does not determine
+employment, institutional ownership, funding, endorsement, study-site status or
+research quality.
+
+## Data and privacy
+
+Only public bibliographic and affiliation metadata is in scope. The pilot does
+not require patient information, clinical data, restricted full text, licensed
+provider exports or credentials stored in monitor state. Staff-level
+performance profiling is prohibited without a separately approved purpose,
+policy and governance process.
+
+## Success and exit
+
+Before a real pilot starts, accountable reviewers must set prospective
+thresholds for sensitivity, positive predictive value, review workload,
+provider reliability and reproducibility. Any released report must be linked to
+validated state and Searchright receipts. False attribution, unexpected data
+collection, provider-policy breach or unrecoverable state triggers rollback.
+
+The machine-readable contract is
+`release/pilots/chhhs-research-intelligence.json`.
